The O3DE lighting investigation's picks
=======================================

A click on the scene, or on a view of a screen-sized resource (a forward target, the depth, the stencil), picks
the pixel there: the surface point the readout inspects, which every such view rings where it projects
(`pickShown`). The lab traces the ray (`trace`); this says what the hit sets.

$[Import* std]$[Import* render_lab_runtime]$[Import* o3de_lighting_values]$[ImportAs rl_runtime rt]

The values a hit sets: the point, its normal turned to face the viewer, and the object. Nothing when the ray
misses (the ceiling's light panel is not a surface the readout inspects).
$[# {_pick click} {caseOption
    {rt::trace {.u click} {.v click} {' "emissive panel"}}
    {^ {} {'}}
    {^ {hit}
        [# n {!if {> {vdot {.normal hit} {.dir hit}} 0.0}
            {vscale {.normal hit} -1.0}
            {.normal hit}}]
        [# p {.point hit}]
        {'
            {setPickShown 1.0}
            {setInspectX {.x p}}
            {setInspectY {.y p}}
            {setInspectZ {.z p}}
            {setInspectNX {.x n}}
            {setInspectNY {.y n}}
            {setInspectNZ {.z n}}
            {setInspectObject {float {.object hit}}}}}}]

Picks the pixel clicked on a view of a screen-sized resource: ringed in every such view, and its surface point
inspected in the scene.
$[# pickPixel {: _pick ClickHandler}]

A click on the scene picks its pixel and inspects its point.
$[# scene {: _pick ClickHandler}]
